              "statements": [
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "P17",
                    "P18"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "On 12 October the Prime Minister welcomed President Trump's announcement of a reciprocal energy ceasefire and told the Commons that President Zelenskyy had assured him Ukraine would implement it as soon as a start date was confirmed."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "P19",
                    "P20",
                    "P3"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "By the Downing Street meeting on 14 October, the government's readout described Russia's attacks on civilians and energy infrastructure since Trump called for the ceasefire, and said the leaders underlined that Russia had no interest in peace. That follows a government spokesperson's response on 10 October to the US-Russia agreement, which said Russia had repeatedly rejected ceasefires."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "N1",
                    "P1",
                    "P14",
                    "P24",
                    "P28"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "Taken together, the week shows London not waiting on Washington's track: more sanctions, military and fiscal packages commissioned for the coming weeks, over 90% of Russia's oil capacity now under UK sanctions, £10 million of missiles brought forward for winter, and the Chancellor pressing partners in Bangkok to copy the UK's LNG shipping ban."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "L1"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "The Scotland speech makes more sense against Burnham's record: Wikidata has him as Mayor of Greater Manchester until June 2026, and as Prime Minister and Minister for the Union since 20 July."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "N2",
                    "P58",
                    "P111",
                    "P113",
                    "P116",
                    "P128"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "He is bringing the mayoral approach to Scotland. He calls the Scottish Government one of Europe's most centralised devolved administrations, points to the buses he had built in Falkirk as the model for all public procurement, and offers Scotland's regions the R\u0026D powers English mayors have, plus localised employment support through DWP devolution. That makes the offer to Holyrood a challenge to its own centralisation as well."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "P84",
                    "P99",
                    "P103"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "Putting Great British Railways' headquarters in Derby fits the same pattern, which Burnham calls 'devolution by default'."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "N3",
                    "P2",
                    "P129",
                    "P46",
                    "P55",
                    "P56"
                  ],
                  "stories": [],
                  "text": "The next month will show whether these plans deliver: the Ukraine packages promised within weeks; the first National Economic Council with the First Ministers, due in a couple of weeks; and the 20 November summit in Brussels. Burnham said the summit deal is more likely if the UK is open to talks on its longer-term relationship with the EU, and that a serious dialogue on the options should follow it."
